---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import Hero from '../components/Hero.astro';
import ContentSection from '../components/ContentSection.astro';
import Callout from '../components/Callout.astro';
import LinkCard from '../components/LinkCard.astro';

const relatedPages = [
  { title: 'Responsible Betting', href: '/responsible-betting', description: 'Staying in control' },
  { title: 'Common Mistakes', href: '/common-betting-mistakes', description: 'Avoiding errors' },
  { title: 'Betting Strategy', href: '/betting-strategy', description: 'Decision framework' },
];
---

<Layout
  title='Why "No Bet" Is Often the Best Decision'
  description="Understanding when passing on a bet is the correct choice and why disciplined bettors say no more often than yes."
>
  <Hero
    title='Why "No Bet" Is Often Best'
    subtitle="The Discipline of Passing on Action"
    size="medium"
  />

  <div class="container content-container">
    <article class="page-content">
      <ContentSection>
        <div class="quick-take">
          <h2>Quick Take</h2>
          <p>
            The most underrated skill in sports betting is knowing when not to bet. Every bet exposes you to the vig, so betting without an edge guarantees long-term losses. Disciplined bettors pass on far more opportunities than they take. Learning to say "no bet" protects your bankroll, preserves your edge for genuine opportunities, and distinguishes serious betting from gambling for entertainment.
          </p>
        </div>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title='Why Is "No Bet" So Important?' id="why">
        <h3>Every bet costs money</h3>
        <p>
          The vig means you're paying for the privilege of betting. Without an edge, each bet has negative expected value. Fewer bets = less vig paid = better long-term results.
        </p>

        <h3>Edge is rare</h3>
        <p>
          Genuine betting edges don't appear every game. Markets are efficient. Finding value requires both analysis and patience—often the analysis concludes "no edge here."
        </p>

        <h3>Action addiction is real</h3>
        <p>
          The desire to have action on games is a form of entertainment seeking that has nothing to do with finding value. Recognizing this urge is the first step to resisting it.
        </p>
      </ContentSection>

      <Callout type="info" title="Passing Is a Decision, Not a Failure">
        <p>
          Choosing not to bet is an active decision based on analysis. It's not missing out—it's protecting your bankroll for when genuine opportunities arise.
        </p>
      </Callout>

      <ContentSection title="When Should You Pass?" id="when-pass">
        <ul>
          <li>When you can't articulate why the bet has value</li>
          <li>When you're betting because you "need action"</li>
          <li>When you're chasing previous losses</li>
          <li>When the line has moved away from your target</li>
          <li>When you haven't done sufficient analysis</li>
          <li>When you're emotional, tired, or impaired</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="What This Means for Bettors" id="what-means">
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Set criteria before looking at games:</strong> Define what constitutes a bet-worthy opportunity.</li>
          <li><strong>Track your pass rate:</strong> If you're betting most games, you're probably not being selective enough.</li>
          <li><strong>Separate entertainment from serious betting:</strong> If you want action for fun, define a separate entertainment budget.</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Key Takeaways" id="takeaways">
        <ul>
          <li>Every bet costs money through the vig</li>
          <li>Genuine edges are rare; most games don't offer value</li>
          <li>Passing is an active decision based on analysis</li>
          <li>Action addiction leads to unnecessary losses</li>
          <li>Disciplined bettors say no more often than yes</li>
        </ul>
      </ContentSection>

      <ContentSection title="Related Resources" id="related">
        <div class="related-grid">
          {relatedPages.map((page) => (
            <LinkCard title={page.title} href={page.href} description={page.description} />
          ))}
        </div>
      </ContentSection>
    </article>
  </div>
</Layout>

<style>
  .page-content { padding: var(--spacing-3xl) 0; }
  .quick-take { background-color: var(--color-surface); border-left: 4px solid var(--color-accent); padding: var(--spacing-lg); border-radius: 0 var(--border-radius) var(--border-radius) 0; margin-bottom: var(--spacing-xl); }
  .quick-take h2 { font-size: 1rem; text-transform: uppercase; letter-spacing: 0.05em; color: var(--color-accent); margin-bottom: var(--spacing-sm); }
  .quick-take p { margin: 0; color: var(--color-text-secondary); }
  .related-grid { display: grid; grid-template-columns: repeat(3, 1fr); gap: var(--spacing-md); margin-top: var(--spacing-lg); }
  @media (max-width: 768px) { .related-grid { grid-template-columns: 1fr; } }
</style>
